### tool_certificate_expire_issue via Moodle's AJAX multi-call endpoint.
### This is the real path the "Expire" button uses (issues-list.js -> core/ajax -> lib/ajax/service.php).
### NOTE: session-cookie authenticated, not token-based.
###   1. Log into the site in your browser as a user who can manage this certificate.
###   2. DevTools > Application/Storage > Cookies > copy the MoodleSession cookie value.
###   3. DevTools > Console > run `M.cfg.sesskey` (or find it in a page's HTML) and copy it.
###   4. Use a DISPOSABLE test issue id, not a real student's (this call permanently expires the issue).
POST https://studentportal.maritimemt.edu.mt/lib/ajax/service.php?sesskey=nm5zviveEK
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: MoodleSession=qroh8o9ag9niaje4dq6da71v0l

[{"index":0,"methodname":"tool_certificate_expire_issue","args":{"id":257}}]

### --- Alternative: classic token-based REST protocol ---
### Only works if 'tool_certificate_expire_issue' has been added to an External Service
### (Site administration > Server > Web services > External services) and a token issued
### for that service. Right now it is NOT: db/services.php declares it with 'ajax' => true
### but no 'services' => [...] entry, so a bare wstoken call will fail with
### "Access control exception" until that's set up.
# POST https://studentportal.maritimemt.edu.mt/webservice/rest/server.php
# Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
#
# wstoken=REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN&wsfunction=tool_certificate_expire_issue&moodlewsrestformat=json&id=257
